2019-10-24","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Tony Thene","x":"There is an impacted supply chain, but we're working hard to offset those challenges by expanding market growth in countries not impacted by the tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/25/carpenter-technology-crs-q1-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRS 2020 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2020-01-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Tim Lain","x":"As a reminder, for most of our business, the impact of changes in raw materials is passed through to our customers via surcharges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/31/carpenter-technology-crs-q2-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRS 2020 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2020-01-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tony Thene","x":"Given the ongoing challenges facing the oil and gas business, especially in North America, we initiated restructuring actions at our Amega West business during the second quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/31/carpenter-technology-crs-q2-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRS 2020 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2020-01-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tim Lain","x":"Operating income in the current second quarter includes $2.3 million of restructuring charges related to our Amega West business as we took actions to rightsize the footprint and cost structure of that business to reflect current market conditions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/31/carpenter-technology-crs-q2-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRS 2020 Q3","e":"crs","d":"2020-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tony Thene","x":"To that end, we have implemented targeted portfolio restructuring and cost reduction initiatives in order to maintain our strong balance sheet.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/carpenter-technology-crs-q3-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRS 2020 Q3","e":"crs","d":"2020-04-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tim Lain","x":"We have already taken actions such as production and maintenance workforce furloughs and a global hiring freeze.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/carpenter-technology-crs-q3-2020-earnings-call-tra.aspx"},{"c":"CRS 2021 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2021-01-28","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Tony R. Thene","x":"As I mentioned earlier, we continue to secure beneficial long-term contracts even during this downturn, with substantial price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/carpenter-technology-corp-crs-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRS 2021 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2021-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tim Lain","x":"Again, the current quarter's results reflect the impact of significantly lower volume, combined with the targeted inventory reduction, partially offset by the cost reduction efforts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/carpenter-technology-corp-crs-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRS 2021 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2021-01-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Tim Lain","x":"The anticipated results reflect incremental operating expense reductions as a result of cost savings actions taken to date, combined with a less pronounced impact of inventory reductions, partially offset by higher sequential depreciation and amortization costs as our global ERP system and hot…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/28/carpenter-technology-corp-crs-q2-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRS 2021 Q3","e":"crs","d":"2021-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Timothy Lain","x":"The current quarter's operating results include $7.6 million of restructuring and asset impairment charges, including inventory writedowns, associated with our ongoing actions to reduce cost and narrow focus in our additive business unit within our PEP segment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/carpenter-technology-corp-crs-q3-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRS 2021 Q3","e":"crs","d":"2021-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Timothy Lain","x":"The operating loss was $40 million in the current quarter when excluding the impact of the special items, namely the restructuring and asset impairment charges and the COVID-19 costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/carpenter-technology-corp-crs-q3-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRS 2021 Q4","e":"crs","d":"2021-07-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Timothy Lain","x":"Third, the current quarter special items include about $3 million of restructuring and asset impairment charges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/29/carpenter-technology-corp-crs-q4-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRS 2021 Q4","e":"crs","d":"2021-07-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Timothy Lain","x":"The restructuring and asset impairment charges, including inventory write-downs, are associated with executing the near final steps against our planned actions to reduce costs and narrow focus in our additive business unit within our PEP segment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/29/carpenter-technology-corp-crs-q4-2021-earnings-cal/"},{"c":"CRS 2025 Q4","e":"crs","d":"2025-07-31","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Gautam Khanna","x":"Just do you think there's any impact to the strong pricing power that you guys have had?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/08/06/carpenter-technology-crs-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRS 2026 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2026-01-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Tony Thene","x":"As evidence of this, we completed three additional long-term agreements with aerospace customers with significant price increases during the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/29/carpenter-tech-crs-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRS 2026 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2026-01-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Tony Thene","x":"I will note again to support our view of the pricing dynamic for our materials, that in the quarter we completed negotiations on three long-term agreements with aerospace customers with significant price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/29/carpenter-tech-crs-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRS 2026 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2026-01-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Tony Thene","x":"Given the supply demand dynamics I just covered, and the visibility, have for the second half of the fiscal year 2026 we are raising our guidance to $680 million to $700 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/29/carpenter-tech-crs-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRS 2026 Q2","e":"crs","d":"2026-01-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Tony Thene","x":"Our increased guidance for fiscal year 2026 implies a 30% to 33% increase over a record fiscal year 2025.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/01/29/carpenter-tech-crs-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRS 2026 Q3","e":"crs","d":"2026-04-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Scott Deuschle","x":"For the transactional price increases that you mentioned in the press release, is that mostly referring to favorable transactional pricing for aerospace structural alloys, or are you seeing those transactional prices creep up more broadly across the portfolio?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/carpenter-crs-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRS 2026 Q3","e":"crs","d":"2026-04-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Tim Lain","x":"We are increasing our outlook for free cash flow and currently expect to generate at least $350 million of adjusted free cash flow in fiscal year 2026.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/29/carpenter-crs-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CRS 2026 Q4","e":"crs","d":"2026-07-30","l":"pri